"""World history answers: civilizations, revolutions, wars, Africa and Rwanda (en/fr/rw/sw). Brief overviews with widely accepted dates; fr/rw/sw are drafts pending fluent review."""
from knowledge_base import _e

ENTRIES_HISTORY = [
_e("agricultural_revolution", ["human_evolution", "ancient_civilizations", "industrial_revolution"],
   ("What was the Agricultural (Neolithic) Revolution?", "Qu'était la révolution agricole (néolithique) ?", "Agricultural (Neolithic) Revolution yari iki?", "Mapinduzi ya Kilimo (Neolithic) yalikuwa nini?"),
   ("agricultural revolution|neolithic revolution|origin of farming|when did farming begin|domestication|beginning of agriculture|hunter gatherers|fertile crescent|first farmers|neolithic",
    "revolution agricole|revolution neolithique|origine de l'agriculture|quand a commence l'agriculture|domestication|debut de l'agriculture|chasseurs cueilleurs|croissant fertile|premiers agriculteurs|neolithique",
    "impinduramatwara y'ubuhinzi|neolithic revolution|inkomoko y'ubuhinzi|ubuhinzi bwatangiye ryari|gutunga amatungo n'ibimera|abahigi|fertile crescent|abahinzi ba mbere|neolithic",
    "mapinduzi ya kilimo|mapinduzi ya neolithic|asili ya kilimo|kilimo kilianza lini|ufugaji na kilimo cha awali|wawindaji|fertile crescent|wakulima wa kwanza|neolithic"),
   ("The Agricultural (Neolithic) Revolution was the shift, beginning about 12,000 years ago, from hunting and gathering to growing crops and herding animals. It began in several places independently, first in the Fertile Crescent (wheat, barley, sheep, goats) and later in China (rice), Mesoamerica (maize), the Andes (potato) and Africa (sorghum, millet, yams).",
    "La révolution agricole (néolithique) est le passage, à partir d'il y a environ 12 000 ans, de la chasse-cueillette à la culture et à l'élevage. Elle a commencé indépendamment en plusieurs endroits, d'abord dans le Croissant fertile (blé, orge, moutons, chèvres), puis en Chine (riz), Mésoamérique (maïs), dans les Andes (pomme de terre) et en Afrique (sorgho, mil, ignames).",
    "Agricultural (Neolithic) Revolution ni impinduka zatangiye hashize imyaka nka 12,000 zo kuva ku guhiga no gutoragura ujya ku buhinzi no korora amatungo. Yatangiye mu bice byinshi ukwabyo, mbere muri Fertile Crescent (ingano, sayiri, intama, ihene), hanyuma mu Bushinwa (umuceri), Mesoamerica (ibigori), Andes (ibirayi) na Afurika (amasaka, uburo, ibijumba).",
    "Mapinduzi ya Kilimo (Neolithic) yalikuwa mabadiliko, kuanzia takriban miaka 12,000 iliyopita, kutoka uwindaji na ukusanyaji kwenda kilimo na ufugaji. Yalianza maeneo kadhaa kwa kujitegemea, kwanza Fertile Crescent (ngano, shayiri, kondoo, mbuzi), baadaye China (mchele), Mesoamerica (mahindi), Andes (viazi) na Afrika (mtama, uwele, viazi vikuu)."),
   (["Farming allowed food surpluses, so people settled in villages and then towns.", "Surplus food allowed specialists (potters, priests, soldiers, scribes), trade, property and governments.", "Costs: more disease from crowded living and animals, harder work, and food shortages after bad harvests.", "This shift led to the first cities and civilizations around 3500–3000 BCE."],
    ["L'agriculture a permis des surplus alimentaires, donc la sédentarisation en villages puis en villes.", "Les surplus ont permis des spécialistes (potiers, prêtres, soldats, scribes), le commerce, la propriété et les États.", "Coûts : plus de maladies (vie en groupe, animaux), travail plus dur, famines après mauvaises récoltes.", "Ce changement a mené aux premières villes et civilisations vers 3500–3000 av. J.-C."],
    ["Ubuhinzi bwatumye hajyaho ibiribwa birenga, abantu batura mu midugudu hanyuma mu mijyi.", "Ibyo birenga byatumye hajyaho abahanga mu mirimo (abubatsi b'inkono, abapadiri, abasirikare, abanditsi), ubucuruzi, umutungo n'ubutegetsi.", "Igiciro: indwara nyinshi kubera guturana n'amatungo, akazi katoroshye, n'inzara nyuma y'isarura ribi.", "Iyo mpinduka yaje kuvamo imijyi ya mbere n'imico ya mbere nka 3500–3000 mbere ya Yesu."],
    ["Kilimo kiliruhusu ziada ya chakula, hivyo watu walikaa vijijini kisha miji.", "Ziada ilileta wataalamu (wafinyanzi, makuhani, askari, waandishi), biashara, mali na serikali.", "Gharama: magonjwa zaidi kwa msongamano na wanyama, kazi ngumu, na njaa baada ya mavuno mabaya.", "Mabadiliko hayo yalisababisha miji na ustaarabu wa kwanza takriban 3500–3000 KK."])),

_e("ancient_civilizations", ["agricultural_revolution", "roman_empire", "african_empires"],
   ("What were the first ancient civilizations? (Mesopotamia, Egypt, Indus, China)", "Quelles furent les premières civilisations antiques ? (Mésopotamie, Égypte, Indus, Chine)", "Imico ya kera ya mbere yari iyihe? (Mesopotamia, Misiri, Indus, Ubushinwa)", "Ustaarabu wa kale wa kwanza ulikuwa upi? (Mesopotamia, Misri, Indus, China)"),
   ("ancient civilizations|mesopotamia|sumer|ancient egypt|pyramids|indus valley|ancient china|first civilizations|cradle of civilization|ancient greece",
    "civilisations antiques|mesopotamie|sumer|egypte antique|pyramides|vallee de l'indus|chine antique|premieres civilisations|berceau de la civilisation|grece antique",
    "imico ya kera|mesopotamia|sumer|misiri ya kera|piramide|indus valley|ubushinwa bwa kera|imico ya mbere|ubugeni bw'imico|ubugereki bwa kera",
    "ustaarabu wa kale|mesopotamia|sumer|misri ya kale|piramidi|bonde la indus|china ya kale|ustaarabu wa kwanza|chimbuko la ustaarabu|ugiriki wa kale"),
   ("The earliest civilizations grew along great rivers where farming was productive: Mesopotamia (Tigris and Euphrates, Sumer, writing by about 3400–3200 BCE), Egypt (the Nile, unified about 3100 BCE), the Indus Valley (about 2600 BCE) and the Yellow River in China. Each developed cities, writing, laws, trade and organised government.",
    "Les premières civilisations se sont développées le long de grands fleuves où l'agriculture était productive : Mésopotamie (Tigre et Euphrate, Sumer, écriture vers 3400–3200 av. J.-C.), Égypte (le Nil, unifiée vers 3100 av. J.-C.), vallée de l'Indus (vers 2600 av. J.-C.) et fleuve Jaune en Chine. Chacune a développé villes, écriture, lois, commerce et gouvernement organisé.",
    "Imico ya mbere yakuriye ku nkombe z'inzuzi nini aho ubuhinzi bwari bwiza: Mesopotamia (Tigris na Euphrates, Sumer, kwandika nka 3400–3200 mbere ya Yesu), Misiri (Nili, yahujwe nka 3100), Indus Valley (nka 2600) n'uruzi rw'Umuhondo mu Bushinwa. Buri umwe wateje imbere imijyi, kwandika, amategeko, ubucuruzi n'ubutegetsi buteguye.",
    "Ustaarabu wa kwanza ulikua kando ya mito mikubwa ambapo kilimo kilikuwa na mazao mengi: Mesopotamia (Tigris na Eufrate, Sumer, uandishi takriban 3400–3200 KK), Misri (Nile, iliunganishwa takriban 3100 KK), Bonde la Indus (takriban 2600 KK) na Mto Manjano China. Kila mmoja ulikuza miji, uandishi, sheria, biashara na serikali iliyopangwa."),
   (["Sumer invented cuneiform writing and the wheel's early use; the Code of Hammurabi (about 1754 BCE, Babylon) is a famous early law code.", "Egypt: pharaohs, hieroglyphs, and the Great Pyramid of Giza (built about 2560 BCE).", "Nubia/Kush (south of Egypt, in today's Sudan) was a powerful African kingdom that even ruled Egypt (25th Dynasty, about 744–656 BCE).", "Greece: city-states like Athens and Sparta; democracy in Athens about 508 BCE; philosophers Socrates, Plato, Aristotle."],
    ["Sumer a inventé l'écriture cunéiforme ; le Code d'Hammurabi (vers 1754 av. J.-C., Babylone) est un célèbre code de lois ancien.", "Égypte : pharaons, hiéroglyphes, et la Grande Pyramide de Gizeh (construite vers 2560 av. J.-C.).", "La Nubie/Koush (au sud de l'Égypte, actuel Soudan) était un puissant royaume africain qui a même dirigé l'Égypte (25e dynastie, vers 744–656 av. J.-C.).", "Grèce : cités-États comme Athènes et Sparte ; démocratie à Athènes vers 508 av. J.-C. ; philosophes Socrate, Platon, Aristote."],
    ["Sumer yahimbye inyandiko za cuneiform; Code ya Hammurabi (nka 1754 mbere ya Yesu, Babylon) ni imwe mu mategeko ya kera azwi.", "Misiri: ba pharaoh, hieroglyphs, na Piramide Nini ya Giza (yubatswe nka 2560 mbere ya Yesu).", "Nubia/Kush (mu majyepfo ya Misiri, Sudani y'ubu) yari ubwami bukomeye bwa Afurika bwategetse na Misiri (25th Dynasty, nka 744–656).", "Ubugereki: imijyi-ibihugu nka Athens na Sparta; demokarasi i Athens nka 508; abahanga Socrates, Plato, Aristotle."],
    ["Sumer ilivumbua uandishi wa cuneiform; Kanuni ya Hammurabi (takriban 1754 KK, Babeli) ni sheria maarufu ya kale.", "Misri: mafarao, hieroglyphs, na Piramidi Kuu ya Giza (ilijengwa takriban 2560 KK).", "Nubia/Kush (kusini mwa Misri, Sudan ya sasa) ulikuwa ufalme wenye nguvu wa Afrika uliotawala hata Misri (Nasaba ya 25, takriban 744–656 KK).", "Ugiriki: majimbo ya miji kama Athens na Sparta; demokrasia Athens takriban 508 KK; wanafalsafa Socrates, Plato, Aristotle."])),

_e("roman_empire", ["ancient_civilizations", "renaissance_science", "world_war_one"],
   ("What was the Roman Empire and why did it fall?", "Qu'était l'Empire romain et pourquoi est-il tombé ?", "Ubwami bw'Abaroma bwari ubuhe kandi kuki bwahirimbanye?", "Himaya ya Roma ilikuwa nini na kwa nini ilianguka?"),
   ("roman empire|rome|fall of rome|why did rome fall|julius caesar|augustus|roman republic|ancient rome|byzantine empire|constantinople",
    "empire romain|rome|chute de rome|pourquoi rome est-elle tombee|jules cesar|auguste|republique romaine|rome antique|empire byzantin|constantinople",
    "ubwami bw'abaroma|roma|kugwa kwa roma|kuki roma yaguye|julius caesar|augustus|repubulika ya roma|roma ya kera|byzantine|constantinople",
    "himaya ya roma|roma|kuanguka kwa roma|kwa nini roma ilianguka|julius caesar|augustus|jamhuri ya roma|roma ya kale|byzantine|constantinople"),
   ("According to tradition Rome was founded in 753 BCE. It became a Republic in 509 BCE and an Empire under Augustus in 27 BCE, eventually ruling the whole Mediterranean. The Western Roman Empire fell in 476 CE; the Eastern (Byzantine) Empire, based in Constantinople, lasted until 1453.",
    "Selon la tradition, Rome fut fondée en 753 av. J.-C. Elle devint République en 509 av. J.-C. puis Empire sous Auguste en 27 av. J.-C., dominant toute la Méditerranée. L'Empire romain d'Occident tomba en 476 ; l'Empire d'Orient (byzantin), basé à Constantinople, dura jusqu'en 1453.",
    "Bivugwa ko Roma yashinzwe mu 753 mbere ya Yesu. Yabaye Repubulika mu 509 hanyuma Ubwami munsi ya Augustus mu 27, itegeka inyanja ya Mediterane yose. Ubwami bw'Abaroma bw'iburengerazuba bwaguye mu 476; ubw'iburasirazuba (Byzantine), bwari i Constantinople, bwamaze kugeza mu 1453.",
    "Kwa mapokeo Roma ilianzishwa 753 KK. Ilikuwa Jamhuri 509 KK na Himaya chini ya Augustus 27 KK, ikitawala Mediterania yote. Himaya ya Roma ya Magharibi ilianguka 476 BK; ya Mashariki (Byzantine), yenye makao Constantinople, ilidumu hadi 1453."),
   (["Julius Caesar was assassinated in 44 BCE; his heir Octavian became Augustus, the first emperor.", "Romans left roads, law, Latin (the root of French, Spanish, Italian), aqueducts and the Colosseum.", "Fall: no single cause. Historians cite civil wars, economic trouble, overstretched borders, plague, and pressure from migrating peoples (Goths, Vandals, Huns).", "The last Western emperor, Romulus Augustulus, was removed in 476; Constantinople fell to the Ottomans in 1453."],
    ["Jules César fut assassiné en 44 av. J.-C. ; son héritier Octave devint Auguste, premier empereur.", "Les Romains ont laissé routes, droit, latin (racine du français, espagnol, italien), aqueducs et Colisée.", "Chute : pas de cause unique. Les historiens citent guerres civiles, difficultés économiques, frontières trop étendues, épidémies et pression de peuples migrants (Goths, Vandales, Huns).", "Le dernier empereur d'Occident, Romulus Augustule, fut déposé en 476 ; Constantinople tomba aux mains des Ottomans en 1453."],
    ["Julius Caesar yarishwe mu 44 mbere ya Yesu; umuragwa we Octavian aba Augustus, umwami wa mbere.", "Abaroma basize imihanda, amategeko, Ikilatini (inkomoko y'Igifaransa, Icyesipanyoli, Igitaliyani), amabarabara y'amazi na Colosseum.", "Kugwa: nta mpamvu imwe. Abahanga bavuga intambara z'abenegihugu, ibibazo by'ubukungu, imipaka yagutse, ibyorezo, n'ingufu z'abimukira (Goths, Vandals, Huns).", "Umwami wa nyuma w'iburengerazuba, Romulus Augustulus, yakuweho mu 476; Constantinople yafashwe n'Abottoman mu 1453."],
    ["Julius Caesar aliuawa 44 KK; mrithi wake Octavian akawa Augustus, mfalme wa kwanza.", "Warumi waliacha barabara, sheria, Kilatini (chanzo cha Kifaransa, Kihispania, Kiitaliano), mifereji ya maji na Colosseum.", "Kuanguka: hakuna sababu moja. Wanahistoria hutaja vita vya wenyewe kwa wenyewe, matatizo ya uchumi, mipaka mipana, tauni, na shinikizo la watu wahamiaji (Goths, Vandals, Huns).", "Mfalme wa mwisho wa Magharibi, Romulus Augustulus, aliondolewa 476; Constantinople ilianguka kwa Waottoman 1453."])),

_e("african_empires", ["ancient_civilizations", "colonialism_slavery", "rwanda_history"],
   ("What were the great African kingdoms and empires? (Mali, Songhai, Aksum, Great Zimbabwe)", "Quels furent les grands royaumes et empires africains ? (Mali, Songhaï, Aksoum, Grand Zimbabwe)", "Ibwami n'ubwami bukomeye bya Afurika bwari ubuhe? (Mali, Songhai, Aksum, Great Zimbabwe)", "Falme na himaya kuu za Afrika zilikuwa zipi? (Mali, Songhai, Aksum, Great Zimbabwe)"),
   ("african empires|african kingdoms|mali empire|mansa musa|songhai empire|timbuktu|aksum|great zimbabwe|ghana empire|african history before colonialism",
    "empires africains|royaumes africains|empire du mali|mansa moussa|empire songhai|tombouctou|aksoum|grand zimbabwe|empire du ghana|histoire africaine avant la colonisation",
    "ubwami bwa afurika|ibwami bya afurika|mali empire|mansa musa|songhai|timbuktu|aksum|great zimbabwe|ghana empire|amateka ya afurika mbere y'ubukoloni",
    "himaya za afrika|falme za afrika|himaya ya mali|mansa musa|himaya ya songhai|timbuktu|aksum|great zimbabwe|himaya ya ghana|historia ya afrika kabla ya ukoloni"),
   ("Africa had many powerful states long before colonial rule. Examples: Kush and Egypt on the Nile; Aksum (Ethiopia/Eritrea, about 100–940 CE), a Christian trading empire; the West African empires of Ghana, Mali (13th–16th centuries) and Songhai (15th–16th centuries); Great Zimbabwe (11th–15th centuries); and kingdoms such as Benin, Kongo, Buganda and Rwanda.",
    "L'Afrique comptait de nombreux États puissants bien avant la colonisation. Exemples : Koush et l'Égypte sur le Nil ; Aksoum (Éthiopie/Érythrée, vers 100–940), empire commerçant chrétien ; les empires ouest-africains du Ghana, du Mali (XIIIe–XVIe siècles) et du Songhaï (XVe–XVIe) ; le Grand Zimbabwe (XIe–XVe) ; et des royaumes comme le Bénin, le Kongo, le Buganda et le Rwanda.",
    "Afurika yari ifite ibihugu bikomeye cyane mbere y'ubukoloni. Ingero: Kush na Misiri ku Nili; Aksum (Etiyopiya/Eritereya, nka 100–940), ubwami bw'ubucuruzi bw'abakristu; ubwami bwa Afurika y'iburengerazuba Ghana, Mali (ikinyejana cya 13–16) na Songhai (15–16); Great Zimbabwe (11–15); n'ibwami nka Benin, Kongo, Buganda n'u Rwanda.",
    "Afrika ilikuwa na dola zenye nguvu kabla ya ukoloni. Mifano: Kush na Misri kando ya Nile; Aksum (Ethiopia/Eritrea, takriban 100–940 BK), himaya ya biashara ya Wakristo; himaya za Afrika Magharibi Ghana, Mali (karne ya 13–16) na Songhai (15–16); Great Zimbabwe (11–15); na falme kama Benin, Kongo, Buganda na Rwanda."),
   (["Mali: Mansa Musa (reigned about 1312–1337) made a famous pilgrimage to Mecca in 1324, spreading news of Mali's gold wealth.", "Timbuktu was a centre of learning, with universities and manuscript libraries still preserved.", "Great Zimbabwe: huge dry-stone city that controlled gold trade with the Indian Ocean coast.", "These states traded gold, salt, ivory and copper across the Sahara and the Indian Ocean."],
    ["Mali : Mansa Moussa (règne vers 1312–1337) fit un célèbre pèlerinage à La Mecque en 1324, révélant la richesse en or du Mali.", "Tombouctou était un centre du savoir, avec universités et bibliothèques de manuscrits encore conservées.", "Grand Zimbabwe : immense cité en pierres sèches contrôlant le commerce de l'or avec la côte de l'océan Indien.", "Ces États commerçaient or, sel, ivoire et cuivre à travers le Sahara et l'océan Indien."],
    ["Mali: Mansa Musa (yategetse nka 1312–1337) yagiye i Mecca mu 1324 azwi cyane, amenyekanisha ubukire bwa Mali mu izahabu.", "Timbuktu yari ikigo cy'ubumenyi, gifite za kaminuza n'amasomero y'inyandiko za kera zikiri zibitswe.", "Great Zimbabwe: umujyi munini w'amabuye atubakishijwe ibumba, wagenzuraga ubucuruzi bw'izahabu n'inkombe y'inyanja y'Abahindi.", "Ibyo bihugu byacuruzaga izahabu, umunyu, amahembe y'inzovu n'umuringa hakoreshejwe Sahara n'inyanja y'Abahindi."],
    ["Mali: Mansa Musa (alitawala takriban 1312–1337) alifanya hija maarufu Makka 1324, akitangaza utajiri wa dhahabu wa Mali.", "Timbuktu ilikuwa kituo cha elimu, chenye vyuo vikuu na maktaba za hati bado zimehifadhiwa.", "Great Zimbabwe: mji mkubwa wa mawe bila chokaa uliodhibiti biashara ya dhahabu na pwani ya Bahari ya Hindi.", "Dola hizi ziliuza dhahabu, chumvi, pembe za ndovu na shaba kuvuka Sahara na Bahari ya Hindi."])),

_e("renaissance_science", ["roman_empire", "industrial_revolution", "french_revolution"],
   ("What was the Renaissance and the Scientific Revolution?", "Qu'étaient la Renaissance et la révolution scientifique ?", "Renaissance na Scientific Revolution byari ibihe?", "Renaissance na Mapinduzi ya Kisayansi yalikuwa nini?"),
   ("renaissance|scientific revolution|enlightenment|leonardo da vinci|galileo|copernicus|isaac newton|printing press|gutenberg|age of enlightenment",
    "renaissance|revolution scientifique|lumieres|leonard de vinci|galilee|copernic|isaac newton|imprimerie|gutenberg|siecle des lumieres",
    "renaissance|scientific revolution|enlightenment|leonardo da vinci|galileo|copernicus|isaac newton|printing press|gutenberg",
    "renaissance|mapinduzi ya kisayansi|enlightenment|leonardo da vinci|galileo|copernicus|isaac newton|mashine ya uchapishaji|gutenberg"),
   ("The Renaissance (about 14th–17th centuries, starting in Italy) was a rebirth of art, learning and curiosity, inspired by classical Greece and Rome. The Scientific Revolution (about 1543–1687) replaced old ideas with observation, experiment and mathematics. The Enlightenment (17th–18th centuries) applied reason to politics and society, promoting rights and liberty.",
    "La Renaissance (environ XIVe–XVIIe siècles, née en Italie) fut une renaissance de l'art, du savoir et de la curiosité, inspirée de la Grèce et de Rome. La révolution scientifique (environ 1543–1687) a remplacé les anciennes idées par l'observation, l'expérience et les mathématiques. Les Lumières (XVIIe–XVIIIe) ont appliqué la raison à la politique et à la société, défendant droits et liberté.",
    "Renaissance (nka ikinyejana cya 14–17, yatangiriye mu Butaliyani) yari ukuvuka bundi bushya kw'ubugeni, ubumenyi n'amatsiko, bishingiye ku Bugereki n'i Roma. Scientific Revolution (nka 1543–1687) yasimbuje ibitekerezo bya kera kureba, igerageza n'imibare. Enlightenment (17–18) yakoresheje ubwenge muri politiki n'imibereho, ishyigikira uburenganzira n'ubwisanzure.",
    "Renaissance (takriban karne ya 14–17, ilianzia Italia) ilikuwa kuzaliwa upya kwa sanaa, elimu na udadisi, kwa kuhamasishwa na Ugiriki na Roma. Mapinduzi ya Kisayansi (takriban 1543–1687) yalibadilisha mawazo ya zamani kwa uchunguzi, majaribio na hisabati. Enlightenment (karne ya 17–18) ilitumia akili katika siasa na jamii, ikikuza haki na uhuru."),
   (["Printing press: Gutenberg, about 1450, spread books and ideas quickly.", "Science: Copernicus (1543, Sun-centred model), Galileo (telescope observations, 1609–10), Newton (laws of motion and gravity, 1687).", "Art: Leonardo da Vinci, Michelangelo, Raphael.", "Enlightenment thinkers (Locke, Voltaire, Rousseau, Montesquieu) influenced the American and French revolutions."],
    ["Imprimerie : Gutenberg, vers 1450, diffuse livres et idées rapidement.", "Science : Copernic (1543, modèle héliocentrique), Galilée (observations à la lunette, 1609–10), Newton (lois du mouvement et gravitation, 1687).", "Art : Léonard de Vinci, Michel-Ange, Raphaël.", "Les penseurs des Lumières (Locke, Voltaire, Rousseau, Montesquieu) ont influencé les révolutions américaine et française."],
    ["Imashini yo gucapa: Gutenberg, nka 1450, yakwirakwije ibitabo n'ibitekerezo vuba.", "Siyansi: Copernicus (1543, izuba rirabagirana hagati), Galileo (telescope, 1609–10), Newton (amategeko y'ingendo na gravity, 1687).", "Ubugeni: Leonardo da Vinci, Michelangelo, Raphael.", "Abatekereza ba Enlightenment (Locke, Voltaire, Rousseau, Montesquieu) bagize ingaruka ku mpinduramatwara za Amerika n'u Bufaransa."],
    ["Mashine ya uchapishaji: Gutenberg, takriban 1450, ilieneza vitabu na mawazo haraka.", "Sayansi: Copernicus (1543, Jua katikati), Galileo (darubini, 1609–10), Newton (sheria za mwendo na mvutano, 1687).", "Sanaa: Leonardo da Vinci, Michelangelo, Raphael.", "Wanafikra wa Enlightenment (Locke, Voltaire, Rousseau, Montesquieu) walishawishi mapinduzi ya Marekani na Ufaransa."])),

_e("colonialism_slavery", ["african_empires", "rwanda_history", "world_war_two"],
   ("What were the transatlantic slave trade and colonialism in Africa? (Berlin Conference, independence)", "Que furent la traite transatlantique et la colonisation de l'Afrique ? (Conférence de Berlin, indépendances)", "Ubucuruzi bw'abacakara n'ubukoloni muri Afurika byari ibiki? (Berlin Conference, ubwigenge)", "Biashara ya utumwa na ukoloni Afrika vilikuwa nini? (Mkutano wa Berlin, uhuru)"),
   ("slave trade|transatlantic slave trade|slavery history|colonialism in africa|scramble for africa|berlin conference|decolonization|african independence|colonization|apartheid",
    "traite des esclaves|traite transatlantique|histoire de l'esclavage|colonisation de l'afrique|partage de l'afrique|conference de berlin|decolonisation|independances africaines|colonisation|apartheid",
    "ubucuruzi bw'abacakara|transatlantic slave trade|amateka y'ubucakara|ubukoloni muri afurika|scramble for africa|berlin conference|decolonization|ubwigenge bwa afurika|ubukoloni|apartheid",
    "biashara ya utumwa|biashara ya utumwa ya atlantiki|historia ya utumwa|ukoloni barani afrika|mgawanyo wa afrika|mkutano wa berlin|kuondoa ukoloni|uhuru wa afrika|ukoloni|ubaguzi wa rangi apartheid"),
   ("From the 1500s to the 1800s, about 12.5 million Africans were forced onto ships in the transatlantic slave trade, and about 10.7 million survived the crossing; millions more were enslaved in other trades. At the Berlin Conference (1884–85) European powers set rules for dividing Africa; by 1914 nearly all of it, except Ethiopia and Liberia, was colonised. Most African countries gained independence between the 1950s and 1970s.",
    "Du XVIe au XIXe siècle, environ 12,5 millions d'Africains furent embarqués de force dans la traite transatlantique, et environ 10,7 millions survécurent à la traversée ; des millions d'autres furent réduits en esclavage dans d'autres traites. À la Conférence de Berlin (1884–85), les puissances européennes fixèrent les règles du partage de l'Afrique ; en 1914 presque tout, sauf l'Éthiopie et le Liberia, était colonisé. La plupart des pays africains ont obtenu l'indépendance entre les années 1950 et 1970.",
    "Kuva mu kinyejana cya 16 kugeza ku cya 19, Abanyafurika nka miliyoni 12.5 bahatiwe kujya mu mato mu bucuruzi bwa transatlantic, nka miliyoni 10.7 barokotse urugendo; abandi miliyoni bahindutse abacakara mu bundi bucuruzi. Muri Berlin Conference (1884–85) ibihugu by'u Burayi byashyizeho amategeko yo gucamo Afurika; mu 1914 hafi yose, usibye Etiyopiya na Liberia, yari yarakolonijwe. Ibihugu byinshi bya Afurika byabonye ubwigenge hagati ya 1950 na 1970.",
    "Kuanzia karne ya 16 hadi 19, takriban Waafrika milioni 12.5 walilazimishwa kuingia meli katika biashara ya utumwa ya Atlantiki, na takriban milioni 10.7 walinusurika safari; mamilioni zaidi walifanywa watumwa kwenye biashara nyingine. Mkutano wa Berlin (1884–85) uliweka kanuni za kugawa Afrika; kufikia 1914 karibu yote, isipokuwa Ethiopia na Liberia, ilikuwa imetawaliwa. Nchi nyingi za Afrika zilipata uhuru kati ya miaka ya 1950 na 1970."),
   (["Britain abolished the slave trade in 1807 and slavery in its empire in 1833–38; the US ended slavery in 1865; Brazil in 1888.", "The slave trade drained Africa of people and wealth and enriched traders and plantation owners in Europe and the Americas.", "Colonial borders were drawn with little regard for existing peoples and kingdoms; this still shapes some African politics.", "Ghana was the first sub-Saharan country to gain independence (1957); Rwanda in 1962; South Africa's apartheid system ended in 1994."],
    ["La Grande-Bretagne a aboli la traite en 1807 et l'esclavage dans son empire en 1833–38 ; les États-Unis en 1865 ; le Brésil en 1888.", "La traite a vidé l'Afrique de ses hommes et de ses richesses et enrichi marchands et planteurs d'Europe et des Amériques.", "Les frontières coloniales ont été tracées sans égard pour les peuples et royaumes existants ; cela marque encore certaines politiques africaines.", "Le Ghana fut le premier pays d'Afrique subsaharienne indépendant (1957) ; le Rwanda en 1962 ; l'apartheid sud-africain a pris fin en 1994."],
    ["Ubwongereza bwakuyeho ubucuruzi bw'abacakara mu 1807 n'ubucakara mu bwami bwabwo mu 1833–38; Amerika mu 1865; Brazil mu 1888.", "Ubucuruzi bw'abacakara bwaranduye Afurika abantu n'ubukire, bukungahaza abacuruzi n'abafite imirima mu Burayi no muri Amerika.", "Imipaka y'abakoloni yashushanyijwe nta kwita ku bantu n'ubwami bwari buhari; ibi biracyagira ingaruka ku bya politiki bimwe muri Afurika.", "Ghana niyo yabaye igihugu cya mbere cya Afurika yo munsi ya Sahara kibonye ubwigenge (1957); u Rwanda mu 1962; apartheid ya Afurika y'Epfo yarangiye mu 1994."],
    ["Uingereza ilikomesha biashara ya utumwa 1807 na utumwa katika himaya yake 1833–38; Marekani 1865; Brazil 1888.", "Biashara ya utumwa ilinyonya Afrika watu na mali, ikatajirisha wafanyabiashara na wamiliki wa mashamba Ulaya na Amerika.", "Mipaka ya kikoloni ilichorwa bila kuzingatia watu na falme zilizokuwepo; hii bado inaathiri siasa za baadhi ya nchi.", "Ghana ilikuwa nchi ya kwanza kusini mwa Sahara kupata uhuru (1957); Rwanda 1962; mfumo wa apartheid Afrika Kusini ulimalizika 1994."])),

_e("industrial_revolution", ["agricultural_revolution", "digital_revolution", "french_revolution"],
   ("What was the Industrial Revolution?", "Qu'était la révolution industrielle ?", "Industrial Revolution yari iki?", "Mapinduzi ya Viwanda yalikuwa nini?"),
   ("industrial revolution|what was the industrial revolution|steam engine|james watt|factories|second industrial revolution|causes of the industrial revolution|textile industry|railways|child labour",
    "revolution industrielle|qu'etait la revolution industrielle|machine a vapeur|james watt|usines|deuxieme revolution industrielle|causes de la revolution industrielle|industrie textile|chemins de fer|travail des enfants",
    "impinduramatwara y'inganda|industrial revolution|moteri y'umwuka|james watt|inganda|impamvu za industrial revolution|inganda z'imyenda|gari ya moshi|imirimo y'abana",
    "mapinduzi ya viwanda|industrial revolution|injini ya mvuke|james watt|viwanda|sababu za mapinduzi ya viwanda|viwanda vya nguo|reli|kazi ya watoto"),
   ("The Industrial Revolution began in Britain around 1760 and spread to Europe and North America. Hand production and animal power gave way to machines, factories and steam power. It started in textiles, then iron, coal and railways. A second phase (about 1870–1914) brought steel, electricity, chemicals and mass production.",
    "La révolution industrielle a commencé en Grande-Bretagne vers 1760 puis s'est étendue à l'Europe et à l'Amérique du Nord. La production manuelle et la force animale ont cédé la place aux machines, aux usines et à la vapeur. Elle a débuté dans le textile, puis le fer, le charbon et les chemins de fer. Une deuxième phase (vers 1870–1914) a apporté acier, électricité, chimie et production de masse.",
    "Industrial Revolution yatangiye mu Bwongereza nka 1760 ikwira mu Burayi no muri Amerika ya Ruguru. Umusaruro w'amaboko n'imbaraga z'amatungo byasimbuwe n'imashini, inganda n'imbaraga z'umwuka (steam). Yatangiriye ku myenda, hanyuma icyuma, amakara na gari ya moshi. Icyiciro cya kabiri (nka 1870–1914) cyazanye ibyuma bikomeye, amashanyarazi, ibinyabutabire n'umusaruro munini.",
    "Mapinduzi ya Viwanda yalianza Uingereza takriban 1760 na kuenea Ulaya na Amerika Kaskazini. Uzalishaji kwa mkono na nguvu za wanyama zilipisha nafasi kwa mashine, viwanda na nguvu ya mvuke. Yalianza kwenye nguo, kisha chuma, makaa na reli. Awamu ya pili (takriban 1870–1914) ilileta chuma-pua, umeme, kemikali na uzalishaji wa wingi."),
   (["Key inventions: spinning jenny (1760s), James Watt's improved steam engine (1769), steam locomotive (1804), telegraph (1830s–40s), Bessemer steel process (1856), electric light (1879).", "Effects: cities grew quickly, living standards rose over time, and the middle class expanded.", "Costs: crowded cities, pollution, dangerous factories, child labour; this led to trade unions and labour laws.", "It also fed demand for raw materials and markets, which drove colonial expansion."],
    ["Inventions clés : spinning jenny (années 1760), machine à vapeur améliorée de Watt (1769), locomotive à vapeur (1804), télégraphe (années 1830–40), procédé Bessemer (1856), lampe électrique (1879).", "Effets : villes en croissance rapide, niveau de vie en hausse à long terme, classe moyenne élargie.", "Coûts : villes surpeuplées, pollution, usines dangereuses, travail des enfants ; d'où syndicats et lois du travail.", "Elle a aussi nourri la demande de matières premières et de marchés, ce qui a stimulé l'expansion coloniale."],
    ["Ibyahimbwe by'ingenzi: spinning jenny (1760), moteri ya Watt yatejwe imbere (1769), gari ya moshi ya steam (1804), telegraph (1830–40), Bessemer steel (1856), itara ry'amashanyarazi (1879).", "Ingaruka: imijyi yakuze vuba, imibereho yazamutse uko igihe gishira, n'icyiciro cy'abaciriritse cyiyongera.", "Ibibi: imijyi yuzuye, umwanda, inganda zishobora guteza ibyago, imirimo y'abana; ibi byatumye habaho sendika n'amategeko y'umurimo.", "Yanazamuye icyifuzo cy'ibikoresho fatizo n'amasoko, bituma ubukoloni bwiyongera."],
    ["Uvumbuzi muhimu: spinning jenny (1760s), injini ya mvuke iliyoboreshwa na Watt (1769), treni ya mvuke (1804), telegrafu (1830–40), mchakato wa Bessemer (1856), taa ya umeme (1879).", "Athari: miji ilikua haraka, viwango vya maisha vilipanda baada ya muda, na tabaka la kati likaongezeka.", "Gharama: miji iliyosongamana, uchafuzi, viwanda hatari, kazi ya watoto; hii ilileta vyama vya wafanyakazi na sheria za kazi.", "Pia iliongeza mahitaji ya malighafi na masoko, na kuchochea upanuzi wa ukoloni."])),

_e("american_revolution", ["french_revolution", "renaissance_science", "colonialism_slavery"],
   ("What was the American Revolution?", "Qu'était la révolution américaine ?", "American Revolution yari iki?", "Mapinduzi ya Marekani yalikuwa nini?"),
   ("american revolution|american war of independence|declaration of independence|1776|thirteen colonies|george washington|boston tea party|us independence|united states founding|no taxation without representation",
    "revolution americaine|guerre d'independance americaine|declaration d'independance|1776|treize colonies|george washington|boston tea party|independance des etats-unis|fondation des etats-unis",
    "american revolution|intambara y'ubwigenge bwa amerika|declaration of independence|1776|colonies cumi n'eshatu|george washington|boston tea party|ubwigenge bwa amerika",
    "mapinduzi ya marekani|vita vya uhuru vya marekani|declaration of independence|1776|makoloni kumi na tatu|george washington|boston tea party|uhuru wa marekani"),
   ("The American Revolution (1775–1783) was the war by which 13 British colonies in North America won independence from Britain. Colonists objected to taxes imposed without their representation in Parliament. The Declaration of Independence was adopted on 4 July 1776, and Britain recognised independence in the Treaty of Paris (1783).",
    "La révolution américaine (1775–1783) fut la guerre par laquelle 13 colonies britanniques d'Amérique du Nord conquirent leur indépendance. Les colons s'opposaient aux impôts décidés sans leur représentation au Parlement. La Déclaration d'indépendance fut adoptée le 4 juillet 1776, et la Grande-Bretagne reconnut l'indépendance par le traité de Paris (1783).",
    "American Revolution (1775–1783) ni intambara yatumye amakoloni 13 y'Abongereza muri Amerika ya Ruguru abona ubwigenge. Abakoloni banze imisoro yashyizweho badahagarariwe muri Parliament. Declaration of Independence yemejwe ku wa 4 Nyakanga 1776, kandi Ubwongereza bwemeye ubwigenge muri Treaty of Paris (1783).",
    "Mapinduzi ya Marekani (1775–1783) yalikuwa vita ambavyo makoloni 13 ya Uingereza Amerika Kaskazini yalipata uhuru kutoka Uingereza. Walowezi walipinga kodi zilizowekwa bila uwakilishi wao Bungeni. Azimio la Uhuru lilipitishwa 4 Julai 1776, na Uingereza ilitambua uhuru kwa Mkataba wa Paris (1783)."),
   (["Trigger events: the Stamp Act (1765), Boston Massacre (1770), Boston Tea Party (1773); fighting began at Lexington and Concord (1775).", "George Washington led the Continental Army; France joined the Americans in 1778, helping win at Yorktown (1781).", "The Constitution (1787) created the federal government; the Bill of Rights (1791) protects individual liberties.", "Its ideas of liberty and republic inspired the French Revolution and later independence movements, although slavery continued in the new nation."],
    ["Événements déclencheurs : Stamp Act (1765), massacre de Boston (1770), Boston Tea Party (1773) ; les combats commencent à Lexington et Concord (1775).", "George Washington dirigea l'armée continentale ; la France rejoignit les Américains en 1778, aidant à gagner à Yorktown (1781).", "La Constitution (1787) créa le gouvernement fédéral ; la Déclaration des droits (1791) protège les libertés individuelles.", "Ses idées de liberté et de république ont inspiré la Révolution française et des mouvements d'indépendance, bien que l'esclavage ait continué dans la nouvelle nation."],
    ["Ibyabaye bitangiza: Stamp Act (1765), Boston Massacre (1770), Boston Tea Party (1773); imirwano yatangiriye i Lexington na Concord (1775).", "George Washington yayoboye Continental Army; u Bufaransa bwifatanyije na Amerika mu 1778, bifasha gutsinda i Yorktown (1781).", "Itegeko Nshinga (1787) ryashyizeho leta ihuriweho; Bill of Rights (1791) irinda uburenganzira bwa buri wese.", "Ibitekerezo byayo by'ubwisanzure na repubulika byahaye imbaraga u Bufaransa n'ibindi bihugu, nubwo ubucakara bwakomeje."],
    ["Matukio ya kuanzisha: Stamp Act (1765), Mauaji ya Boston (1770), Boston Tea Party (1773); mapigano yalianza Lexington na Concord (1775).", "George Washington aliongoza Jeshi la Bara; Ufaransa ilijiunga na Wamarekani 1778, ikisaidia kushinda Yorktown (1781).", "Katiba (1787) iliunda serikali ya shirikisho; Mswada wa Haki (1791) hulinda uhuru wa mtu binafsi.", "Mawazo yake ya uhuru na jamhuri yalihamasisha Mapinduzi ya Ufaransa na harakati za uhuru, ingawa utumwa uliendelea nchini humo."])),

_e("french_revolution", ["american_revolution", "russian_revolution", "renaissance_science"],
   ("What was the French Revolution?", "Qu'était la Révolution française ?", "French Revolution yari iki?", "Mapinduzi ya Ufaransa yalikuwa nini?"),
   ("french revolution|storming of the bastille|bastille|napoleon|napoleon bonaparte|louis xvi|marie antoinette|reign of terror|declaration of the rights of man|1789",
    "revolution francaise|prise de la bastille|bastille|napoleon|napoleon bonaparte|louis xvi|marie antoinette|la terreur|declaration des droits de l'homme|1789",
    "impinduramatwara y'abafaransa|french revolution|gufata bastille|bastille|napoleon|napoleon bonaparte|louis xvi|marie antoinette|reign of terror|1789",
    "mapinduzi ya ufaransa|french revolution|kuvamiwa kwa bastille|bastille|napoleon|napoleon bonaparte|louis xvi|marie antoinette|utawala wa hofu|1789"),
   ("The French Revolution (1789–1799) overthrew the absolute monarchy and the privileges of the nobility and clergy. Causes included debt, unfair taxes, food shortages and Enlightenment ideas. The Bastille fortress was stormed on 14 July 1789, and the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen (August 1789) proclaimed liberty and equality before the law.",
    "La Révolution française (1789–1799) a renversé la monarchie absolue et les privilèges de la noblesse et du clergé. Causes : dettes, impôts injustes, pénuries alimentaires et idées des Lumières. La Bastille fut prise le 14 juillet 1789, et la Déclaration des droits de l'homme et du citoyen (août 1789) proclama la liberté et l'égalité devant la loi.",
    "French Revolution (1789–1799) yahiritse ubwami bwuzuye n'ibyiza by'abanyacyubahiro n'abapadiri. Impamvu: imyenda, imisoro itari iy'ukuri, inzara n'ibitekerezo bya Enlightenment. Bastille yafashwe ku wa 14 Nyakanga 1789, na Declaration of the Rights of Man (Kanama 1789) yatangaje ubwisanzure no kunganya imbere y'amategeko.",
    "Mapinduzi ya Ufaransa (1789–1799) yaliangusha ufalme kamili na upendeleo wa waungwana na makasisi. Sababu: madeni, kodi zisizo za haki, uhaba wa chakula na mawazo ya Enlightenment. Ngome ya Bastille ilivamiwa 14 Julai 1789, na Azimio la Haki za Binadamu na Raia (Agosti 1789) lilitangaza uhuru na usawa mbele ya sheria."),
   (["King Louis XVI was executed in January 1793; France became a republic.", "The Reign of Terror (1793–94), led by Robespierre, sent about 17,000 people to the guillotine by official sentence, and many more died in prisons and revolts.", "Napoleon Bonaparte seized power in 1799 and became Emperor in 1804; he fell in 1815 at Waterloo.", "Legacy: citizenship, secular law (the Napoleonic Code), the metric system, and ideas of national sovereignty."],
    ["Louis XVI fut exécuté en janvier 1793 ; la France devint une république.", "La Terreur (1793–94), menée par Robespierre, envoya environ 17 000 personnes à la guillotine par condamnation officielle, et beaucoup d'autres moururent en prison ou lors de révoltes.", "Napoléon Bonaparte prit le pouvoir en 1799, devint empereur en 1804 et tomba en 1815 à Waterloo.", "Héritage : citoyenneté, droit laïque (Code civil), système métrique et idée de souveraineté nationale."],
    ["Umwami Louis XVI yishwe muri Mutarama 1793; u Bufaransa bwabaye repubulika.", "Reign of Terror (1793–94), yayobowe na Robespierre, yohereje abantu nka 17,000 kuri guillotine hakurikijwe imanza, n'abandi benshi bapfiriye muri gereza no mu myivumbagatanyo.", "Napoleon Bonaparte yafashe ubutegetsi mu 1799, aba Emperor mu 1804; yaguye mu 1815 i Waterloo.", "Umurage: ubwenegihugu, amategeko atari aya kiliziya (Code Napoléon), metric system n'igitekerezo cy'ubusugire bw'igihugu."],
    ["Mfalme Louis XVI aliuawa Januari 1793; Ufaransa ikawa jamhuri.", "Utawala wa Hofu (1793–94), ulioongozwa na Robespierre, ulituma takriban watu 17,000 kwenye guillotine kwa hukumu rasmi, na wengi zaidi walikufa gerezani na kwenye ghasia.", "Napoleon Bonaparte alishika madaraka 1799, akawa Mfalme 1804; alianguka 1815 Waterloo.", "Urithi: uraia, sheria za kidunia (Kanuni ya Napoleon), mfumo wa metri, na wazo la uhuru wa taifa."])),

_e("russian_revolution", ["world_war_one", "cold_war", "french_revolution"],
   ("What was the Russian Revolution of 1917?", "Qu'était la révolution russe de 1917 ?", "Russian Revolution ya 1917 yari iki?", "Mapinduzi ya Urusi ya 1917 yalikuwa nini?"),
   ("russian revolution|1917 revolution|bolsheviks|lenin|october revolution|tsar nicholas|soviet union|ussr|stalin|communism",
    "revolution russe|revolution de 1917|bolcheviks|lenine|revolution d'octobre|tsar nicolas|union sovietique|urss|staline|communisme",
    "impinduramatwara y'abarusiya|russian revolution|1917|bolsheviks|lenin|october revolution|tsar nicholas|soviet union|ussr|stalin|communism",
    "mapinduzi ya urusi|mapinduzi ya 1917|bolsheviks|lenin|mapinduzi ya oktoba|tsar nicholas|umoja wa kisovieti|ussr|stalin|ukomunisti"),
   ("The Russian Revolution of 1917 happened in two stages. In February (March by the modern calendar) protests, war weariness and food shortages forced Tsar Nicholas II to abdicate, ending 300 years of Romanov rule. In October (November) the Bolsheviks, led by Vladimir Lenin, seized power from the weak Provisional Government. A civil war followed (1918–1922), and the Soviet Union (USSR) was founded in 1922.",
    "La révolution russe de 1917 s'est déroulée en deux temps. En février (mars selon le calendrier actuel), manifestations, lassitude de la guerre et pénuries ont forcé le tsar Nicolas II à abdiquer, mettant fin à 300 ans de règne des Romanov. En octobre (novembre), les bolcheviks de Lénine ont pris le pouvoir au fragile gouvernement provisoire. Une guerre civile suivit (1918–1922) et l'Union soviétique (URSS) fut fondée en 1922.",
    "Russian Revolution ya 1917 yabaye mu byiciro bibiri. Muri Gashyantare (Werurwe ukurikije kalendari ya none) imyigaragambyo, kunanirwa intambara n'inzara byahatiye Tsar Nicholas II kwegura, birangiza imyaka 300 y'ingoma ya Romanov. Muri Ukwakira (Ugushyingo) Bolsheviks bayobowe na Vladimir Lenin bafashe ubutegetsi ku butegetsi bw'agateganyo bworoshye. Hakurikiyeho intambara y'abenegihugu (1918–1922), maze Soviet Union (USSR) ishingwa mu 1922.",
    "Mapinduzi ya Urusi ya 1917 yalitokea katika hatua mbili. Februari (Machi kwa kalenda ya sasa) maandamano, uchovu wa vita na uhaba wa chakula vilimlazimisha Tsar Nicholas II kujiuzulu, na kumaliza miaka 300 ya utawala wa Romanov. Oktoba (Novemba) Bolsheviks wakiongozwa na Vladimir Lenin walichukua madaraka kutoka Serikali ya Muda dhaifu. Vita vya wenyewe kwa wenyewe vilifuata (1918–1922), na Umoja wa Kisovieti (USSR) ukaanzishwa 1922."),
   (["Bolshevik promises: 'Peace, Land and Bread'; Russia left World War I with the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk (1918).", "Tsar Nicholas II and his family were killed in 1918.", "After Lenin died (1924), Joseph Stalin took control; his rule brought rapid industrialisation but also purges, forced collectivisation, famine and the Gulag camps, killing millions.", "The USSR became a superpower and Cold War rival of the USA until it dissolved in 1991."],
    ["Promesses bolcheviques : « Paix, terre et pain » ; la Russie quitta la Première Guerre par le traité de Brest-Litovsk (1918).", "Le tsar Nicolas II et sa famille furent tués en 1918.", "Après la mort de Lénine (1924), Joseph Staline prit le contrôle ; son règne apporta industrialisation rapide mais aussi purges, collectivisation forcée, famine et goulags, faisant des millions de morts.", "L'URSS devint une superpuissance et rivale des États-Unis pendant la guerre froide jusqu'à sa dissolution en 1991."],
    ["Amasezerano ya Bolshevik: «Amahoro, Ubutaka n'Umugati»; u Burusiya bwavuye mu ntambara ya mbere y'isi binyuze muri Brest-Litovsk (1918).", "Tsar Nicholas II n'umuryango we bishwe mu 1918.", "Nyuma y'urupfu rwa Lenin (1924), Joseph Stalin yafashe ubutegetsi; ingoma ye yazanye inganda vuba ariko n'ibihano, guhatira ubuhinzi rusange, inzara na gulag, byishe miliyoni.", "USSR yabaye igihugu gikomeye n'umunyamuhari wa USA mu Cold War kugeza isenyutse mu 1991."],
    ["Ahadi za Bolshevik: 'Amani, Ardhi na Mkate'; Urusi ilitoka Vita vya Kwanza vya Dunia kwa Mkataba wa Brest-Litovsk (1918).", "Tsar Nicholas II na familia yake waliuawa 1918.", "Lenin alipofariki (1924), Joseph Stalin alichukua udhibiti; utawala wake ulileta viwanda haraka lakini pia usafishaji, kilimo cha lazima cha pamoja, njaa na kambi za Gulag, zikiua mamilioni.", "USSR ikawa dola kuu na mpinzani wa Marekani katika Vita Baridi hadi ilipovunjika 1991."])),

_e("world_war_one", ["world_war_two", "russian_revolution", "roman_empire"],
   ("What caused World War I and how did it end?", "Quelles furent les causes de la Première Guerre mondiale et comment s'est-elle terminée ?", "Intambara ya mbere y'isi yatewe n'iki kandi yarangiye ite?", "Vita vya Kwanza vya Dunia vilisababishwa na nini na viliishaje?"),
   ("world war 1|world war one|first world war|ww1|wwi|causes of world war 1|archduke franz ferdinand|treaty of versailles|trench warfare|1914",
    "premiere guerre mondiale|guerre de 14-18|ww1|causes de la premiere guerre mondiale|archiduc francois-ferdinand|traite de versailles|guerre des tranchees|1914",
    "intambara ya mbere y'isi|ww1|impamvu z'intambara ya mbere y'isi|franz ferdinand|treaty of versailles|trench warfare|1914",
    "vita vya kwanza vya dunia|ww1|sababu za vita vya kwanza vya dunia|franz ferdinand|mkataba wa versailles|vita vya mahandaki|1914"),
   ("World War I (1914–1918) was fought mainly between the Allied Powers (France, Britain, Russia, later Italy and the USA) and the Central Powers (Germany, Austria-Hungary, the Ottoman Empire, Bulgaria). The spark was the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria in Sarajevo on 28 June 1914, but deeper causes included militarism, alliances, imperial rivalry and nationalism. Roughly 9–10 million soldiers and millions of civilians died.",
    "La Première Guerre mondiale (1914–1918) opposa surtout les Alliés (France, Royaume-Uni, Russie, puis Italie et États-Unis) aux Puissances centrales (Allemagne, Autriche-Hongrie, Empire ottoman, Bulgarie). L'étincelle fut l'assassinat de l'archiduc François-Ferdinand à Sarajevo le 28 juin 1914, mais les causes profondes étaient le militarisme, les alliances, les rivalités impériales et le nationalisme. Environ 9 à 10 millions de soldats et des millions de civils sont morts.",
    "Intambara ya mbere y'isi (1914–1918) yarwanywe hagati y'Allied Powers (u Bufaransa, u Bwongereza, u Burusiya, hanyuma u Butaliyani na USA) na Central Powers (Ubudage, Autriche-Hongrie, Ubwami bw'Abottoman, Bulgaria). Intandaro ni iyicwa rya Archduke Franz Ferdinand i Sarajevo ku wa 28 Kamena 1914, ariko impamvu zihariye zari militarism, ubumwe bw'ibihugu, ihangana ry'abakoloni na nationalism. Abasirikare nka miliyoni 9–10 n'abasivili benshi barapfuye.",
    "Vita vya Kwanza vya Dunia (1914–1918) vilipiganwa hasa kati ya Washirika (Ufaransa, Uingereza, Urusi, baadaye Italia na Marekani) na Madola ya Kati (Ujerumani, Austria-Hungary, Dola ya Ottoman, Bulgaria). Cheche ilikuwa kuuawa kwa Archduke Franz Ferdinand Sarajevo 28 Juni 1914, lakini sababu za kina ni ujeshi, miungano, ushindani wa kikoloni na utaifa. Takriban wanajeshi milioni 9–10 na mamilioni ya raia walikufa."),
   (["Ended with the armistice on 11 November 1918; the Treaty of Versailles (1919) blamed Germany and imposed reparations.", "New technology: machine guns, poison gas, tanks, aircraft, submarines; trench warfare caused long stalemates.", "Four empires collapsed: German, Austro-Hungarian, Russian and Ottoman.", "The League of Nations was created to keep peace but failed to prevent World War II; German resentment of Versailles contributed to the rise of the Nazis."],
    ["Fin avec l'armistice du 11 novembre 1918 ; le traité de Versailles (1919) rendit l'Allemagne responsable et imposa des réparations.", "Nouvelles techniques : mitrailleuses, gaz toxiques, chars, avions, sous-marins ; la guerre de tranchées causa de longues impasses.", "Quatre empires s'effondrèrent : allemand, austro-hongrois, russe et ottoman.", "La Société des Nations fut créée pour garantir la paix mais n'a pas empêché la Seconde Guerre ; le ressentiment allemand envers Versailles a favorisé la montée des nazis."],
    ["Yarangiye n'agahenge ku wa 11 Ugushyingo 1918; Treaty of Versailles (1919) yashinje Ubudage ishyiraho indishyi.", "Ikoranabuhanga rishya: imbunda zihuta, imyuka y'ubumara, tanks, indege, ubwato bwo mu mazi; trench warfare yateje guhagarara igihe kirekire.", "Ubwami bune bwarasenyutse: Ubudage, Autriche-Hongrie, Uburusiya n'Abottoman.", "League of Nations yashyizweho kurinda amahoro ariko ntiyabujije Intambara ya kabiri; uburakari bw'Abadage kuri Versailles bwagize uruhare mu izamuka rya Nazi."],
    ["Viliisha kwa mkataba wa kusitisha mapigano 11 Novemba 1918; Mkataba wa Versailles (1919) uliilaumu Ujerumani na kuweka fidia.", "Teknolojia mpya: bunduki za rashasha, gesi ya sumu, vifaru, ndege, manowari; vita vya mahandaki vilileta mkwamo mrefu.", "Himaya nne zilianguka: Ujerumani, Austria-Hungary, Urusi na Ottoman.", "Ligi ya Mataifa iliundwa kulinda amani lakini haikuzuia Vita vya Pili; chuki ya Wajerumani kwa Versailles ilichangia kupanda kwa Nazi."])),

_e("world_war_two", ["world_war_one", "cold_war", "colonialism_slavery"],
   ("What was World War II (causes, key events, how it ended)?", "Qu'était la Seconde Guerre mondiale (causes, événements clés, fin) ?", "Intambara ya kabiri y'isi yari iki (impamvu, ibyabaye, uko yarangiye)?", "Vita vya Pili vya Dunia vilikuwa nini (sababu, matukio, jinsi viliisha)?"),
   ("world war 2|world war two|second world war|ww2|wwii|causes of world war 2|hitler|nazi germany|holocaust|atomic bomb|hiroshima|d-day",
    "seconde guerre mondiale|guerre de 39-45|ww2|causes de la seconde guerre mondiale|hitler|allemagne nazie|holocauste|bombe atomique|hiroshima|jour j",
    "intambara ya kabiri y'isi|ww2|impamvu z'intambara ya kabiri y'isi|hitler|ubudage bwa nazi|holocaust|bombe atomique|hiroshima|d-day",
    "vita vya pili vya dunia|ww2|sababu za vita vya pili vya dunia|hitler|ujerumani ya nazi|holocaust|bomu la atomiki|hiroshima|d-day"),
   ("World War II (1939–1945) was the deadliest war in history, with an estimated 70–85 million deaths. It began on 1 September 1939 when Nazi Germany under Adolf Hitler invaded Poland. It was fought between the Allies (Britain, the Soviet Union, the USA, China, France and others) and the Axis (Germany, Italy, Japan). Causes included the Treaty of Versailles, the Great Depression, aggressive nationalism and the failure of appeasement.",
    "La Seconde Guerre mondiale (1939–1945) fut la guerre la plus meurtrière de l'histoire, avec environ 70 à 85 millions de morts. Elle a commencé le 1er septembre 1939 quand l'Allemagne nazie d'Adolf Hitler a envahi la Pologne. Elle opposa les Alliés (Royaume-Uni, URSS, États-Unis, Chine, France et autres) à l'Axe (Allemagne, Italie, Japon). Causes : traité de Versailles, Grande Dépression, nationalisme agressif, échec de l'apaisement.",
    "Intambara ya kabiri y'isi (1939–1945) niyo yishe abantu benshi mu mateka, abagera kuri miliyoni 70–85. Yatangiye ku wa 1 Nzeri 1939 ubwo Ubudage bwa Nazi bwa Adolf Hitler bwateraga Pologne. Yarwanywe hagati y'Allies (Ubwongereza, USSR, USA, Ubushinwa, u Bufaransa n'abandi) n'Axis (Ubudage, u Butaliyani, Ubuyapani). Impamvu: Treaty of Versailles, Great Depression, nationalism y'ubukana no gutsindwa kwa appeasement.",
    "Vita vya Pili vya Dunia (1939–1945) vilikuwa vita vilivyoua zaidi katika historia, takriban vifo milioni 70–85. Vilianza 1 Septemba 1939 Ujerumani ya Nazi chini ya Adolf Hitler ilipovamia Poland. Vilipiganwa kati ya Washirika (Uingereza, USSR, Marekani, China, Ufaransa na wengine) na Axis (Ujerumani, Italia, Japani). Sababu: Mkataba wa Versailles, Mdororo Mkuu, utaifa mkali na kushindwa kwa appeasement."),
   (["The Holocaust: Nazi Germany and its collaborators murdered about six million Jews and millions of others (Roma, disabled people, political prisoners).", "Turning points: Battle of Stalingrad (1942–43), D-Day landings in Normandy (6 June 1944), Soviet advance to Berlin.", "Germany surrendered on 8 May 1945; the US dropped atomic bombs on Hiroshima (6 August) and Nagasaki (9 August); Japan surrendered on 2 September 1945.", "Aftermath: the United Nations (1945), decolonisation, the Cold War and the division of Europe."],
    ["L'Holocauste : l'Allemagne nazie et ses collaborateurs ont assassiné environ six millions de Juifs et des millions d'autres personnes (Roms, handicapés, prisonniers politiques).", "Tournants : bataille de Stalingrad (1942–43), débarquement de Normandie (6 juin 1944), avancée soviétique vers Berlin.", "L'Allemagne capitula le 8 mai 1945 ; les États-Unis larguèrent des bombes atomiques sur Hiroshima (6 août) et Nagasaki (9 août) ; le Japon capitula le 2 septembre 1945.", "Suites : ONU (1945), décolonisation, guerre froide et division de l'Europe."],
    ["Holocaust: Ubudage bwa Nazi n'abafatanyije nabwo bishe Abayahudi nka miliyoni esheshatu na miliyoni z'abandi (Roma, abafite ubumuga, imfungwa za politiki).", "Ibihe by'impinduka: Intambara ya Stalingrad (1942–43), D-Day muri Normandy (6 Kamena 1944), Abasoviyeti bagana i Berlin.", "Ubudage bwarishyize ku wa 8 Gicurasi 1945; USA yajugunye bombe za atomique kuri Hiroshima (6 Kanama) na Nagasaki (9 Kanama); Ubuyapani bwishyize ku wa 2 Nzeri 1945.", "Ingaruka: UN (1945), decolonisation, Cold War no kugabana kw'u Burayi."],
    ["Holocaust: Ujerumani ya Nazi na washirika wake waliua takriban Wayahudi milioni sita na mamilioni ya wengine (Roma, walemavu, wafungwa wa kisiasa).", "Mabadiliko makuu: Vita vya Stalingrad (1942–43), kutua Normandy D-Day (6 Juni 1944), Wasovieti kuelekea Berlin.", "Ujerumani ilijisalimisha 8 Mei 1945; Marekani ilidondosha mabomu ya atomiki Hiroshima (6 Agosti) na Nagasaki (9 Agosti); Japani ilijisalimisha 2 Septemba 1945.", "Matokeo: Umoja wa Mataifa (1945), kuondoa ukoloni, Vita Baridi na kugawanywa kwa Ulaya."])),

_e("cold_war", ["world_war_two", "russian_revolution", "digital_revolution"],
   ("What was the Cold War?", "Qu'était la guerre froide ?", "Cold War yari iki?", "Vita Baridi vilikuwa nini?"),
   ("cold war|what was the cold war|berlin wall|cuban missile crisis|space race|arms race|nato|warsaw pact|iron curtain|fall of the soviet union|vietnam war|korean war",
    "guerre froide|qu'etait la guerre froide|mur de berlin|crise des missiles de cuba|course a l'espace|course aux armements|otan|pacte de varsovie|rideau de fer|chute de l'urss|guerre du vietnam|guerre de coree",
    "cold war|intambara y'ubukonje|urukuta rwa berlin|cuban missile crisis|space race|arms race|nato|warsaw pact|iron curtain|isenyuka rya ussr|intambara ya vietnam",
    "vita baridi|cold war|ukuta wa berlin|mgogoro wa makombora ya cuba|mbio za anga|mbio za silaha|nato|warsaw pact|pazia la chuma|kuanguka kwa ussr|vita vya vietnam"),
   ("The Cold War (about 1947–1991) was a long rivalry between the United States (capitalist democracy, NATO) and the Soviet Union (communist, Warsaw Pact) that never became direct war between them. They competed through arms, spies, propaganda, the space race and 'proxy wars' such as Korea (1950–53) and Vietnam. The Cuban Missile Crisis (1962) was the closest the world came to nuclear war.",
    "La guerre froide (environ 1947–1991) fut une longue rivalité entre les États-Unis (démocratie capitaliste, OTAN) et l'Union soviétique (communiste, pacte de Varsovie), qui ne dégénéra jamais en guerre directe entre eux. Ils se sont affrontés par les armements, l'espionnage, la propagande, la course à l'espace et des « guerres par procuration » comme la Corée (1950–53) et le Vietnam. La crise des missiles de Cuba (1962) fut le moment le plus proche d'une guerre nucléaire.",
    "Cold War (nka 1947–1991) yari ihangana rirerire hagati ya USA (demokarasi ya capitalist, NATO) na Soviet Union (communist, Warsaw Pact) ritigeze rihinduka intambara itaziguye hagati yabo. Bahanganye mu ntwaro, ubutasi, propaganda, space race n'intambara zihagarariwe nka Koreya (1950–53) na Vietnam. Cuban Missile Crisis (1962) niyo yegereye cyane intambara ya nucléaire.",
    "Vita Baridi (takriban 1947–1991) vilikuwa ushindani mrefu kati ya Marekani (demokrasia ya kibepari, NATO) na Umoja wa Kisovieti (ukomunisti, Warsaw Pact) ambao haukuwa vita vya moja kwa moja kati yao. Walishindana kwa silaha, ujasusi, propaganda, mbio za anga na 'vita vya wakala' kama Korea (1950–53) na Vietnam. Mgogoro wa Makombora ya Cuba (1962) ulikuwa karibu zaidi na vita vya nyuklia."),
   (["Berlin was divided; the Berlin Wall stood from 1961 to 1989, and its fall (9 November 1989) symbolised the end of the division.", "Space race: Sputnik (1957), Yuri Gagarin first human in space (1961), Apollo 11 Moon landing (1969).", "Many African and Asian countries became Cold War battlegrounds; the Non-Aligned Movement tried to stay neutral.", "Germany reunified in 1990 and the Soviet Union dissolved in December 1991, ending the Cold War."],
    ["Berlin fut divisée ; le mur de Berlin exista de 1961 à 1989, et sa chute (9 novembre 1989) symbolisa la fin de la division.", "Course à l'espace : Spoutnik (1957), Youri Gagarine premier humain dans l'espace (1961), alunissage d'Apollo 11 (1969).", "De nombreux pays africains et asiatiques devinrent des terrains d'affrontement ; le Mouvement des non-alignés tenta de rester neutre.", "L'Allemagne se réunifia en 1990 et l'Union soviétique se dissout en décembre 1991, mettant fin à la guerre froide."],
    ["Berlin yacitsemo kabiri; Urukuta rwa Berlin rwabayeho 1961–1989, kugwa kwarwo (9 Ugushyingo 1989) byerekanye iherezo ry'ubwo bwigunge.", "Space race: Sputnik (1957), Yuri Gagarin umuntu wa mbere mu cyogajuru (1961), Apollo 11 ku kwezi (1969).", "Ibihugu byinshi bya Afurika na Aziya byabaye ahantu h'imirwano; Non-Aligned Movement yagerageje kutabogamira.", "Ubudage bwongeye guhurira mu 1990 maze Soviet Union isenyuka mu Kuboza 1991, birangiza Cold War."],
    ["Berlin iligawanywa; Ukuta wa Berlin ulisimama 1961–1989, kuanguka kwake (9 Novemba 1989) kuliashiria mwisho wa mgawanyiko.", "Mbio za anga: Sputnik (1957), Yuri Gagarin binadamu wa kwanza angani (1961), Apollo 11 mwezini (1969).", "Nchi nyingi za Afrika na Asia zikawa uwanja wa mapambano; Harakati ya Kutofungamana ilijaribu kubaki upande wowote.", "Ujerumani iliungana 1990 na Umoja wa Kisovieti ulivunjika Desemba 1991, ukimaliza Vita Baridi."])),

_e("rwanda_history", ["colonialism_slavery", "african_empires", "rwanda_basics"],
   ("What is the history of Rwanda? (kingdom, colonial period, 1994 genocide against the Tutsi, today)", "Quelle est l'histoire du Rwanda ? (royaume, colonisation, génocide contre les Tutsi de 1994, aujourd'hui)", "Amateka y'u Rwanda ni ayahe? (ubwami, ubukoloni, jenoside yakorewe Abatutsi 1994, uyu munsi)", "Historia ya Rwanda ni ipi? (ufalme, ukoloni, mauaji ya halaiki dhidi ya Watutsi 1994, leo)"),
   ("history of rwanda|rwanda history|rwandan history|rwanda genocide|genocide against the tutsi|1994 genocide|kwibuka|rwanda independence|rwanda kingdom|rwanda colonial|paul kagame|rpf",
    "histoire du rwanda|histoire rwandaise|genocide du rwanda|genocide contre les tutsi|genocide de 1994|kwibuka|independance du rwanda|royaume du rwanda|colonisation du rwanda|paul kagame|fpr",
    "amateka y'u rwanda|amateka y'abanyarwanda|jenoside mu rwanda|jenoside yakorewe abatutsi|jenoside ya 1994|kwibuka|ubwigenge bw'u rwanda|ubwami bw'u rwanda|ubukoloni mu rwanda|paul kagame|rpf|inkotanyi",
    "historia ya rwanda|historia ya kinyarwanda|mauaji ya halaiki rwanda|mauaji ya halaiki dhidi ya watutsi|mauaji ya 1994|kwibuka|uhuru wa rwanda|ufalme wa rwanda|ukoloni rwanda|paul kagame|rpf"),
   ("Rwanda was a centralised kingdom for centuries, ruled by a mwami and unified by Kinyarwanda language and culture. It was colonised by Germany (from about 1897) and, after World War I, administered by Belgium, which hardened ethnic identity cards that divided Hutu, Tutsi and Twa. Rwanda became independent on 1 July 1962. Between 7 April and mid-July 1994, the Genocide against the Tutsi killed at least 800,000 people (estimates range higher); it ended when the Rwandan Patriotic Front took control, on 4 July in Kigali.",
    "Le Rwanda fut pendant des siècles un royaume centralisé, dirigé par un mwami et uni par la langue et la culture kinyarwanda. Il fut colonisé par l'Allemagne (vers 1897) puis, après la Première Guerre mondiale, administré par la Belgique, qui durcit les cartes d'identité ethniques divisant Hutu, Tutsi et Twa. Le Rwanda devint indépendant le 1er juillet 1962. Entre le 7 avril et mi-juillet 1994, le génocide contre les Tutsi a tué au moins 800 000 personnes (des estimations vont plus haut) ; il a pris fin quand le Front patriotique rwandais a pris le contrôle, le 4 juillet à Kigali.",
    "U Rwanda rwari ubwami buhuriweho mu binyejana byinshi, buyobowe n'umwami kandi buhuriye ku rurimi n'umuco by'Ikinyarwanda. Rwakolonijwe n'u Budage (nka 1897) hanyuma, nyuma y'Intambara ya mbere y'isi, ruyoborwa n'u Bubiligi, bwakomeje indangamuntu zishingiye ku moko zigabanya Abahutu, Abatutsi n'Abatwa. U Rwanda rwabonye ubwigenge ku wa 1 Nyakanga 1962. Hagati ya 7 Mata n'impera ya Nyakanga 1994, Jenoside yakorewe Abatutsi yahitanye nibura abantu 800,000 (ibigereranyo bimwe bivuga benshi kurushaho); yarangiye ubwo Rwandan Patriotic Front yafataga igihugu, ku wa 4 Nyakanga i Kigali.",
    "Rwanda ilikuwa ufalme uliounganishwa kwa karne nyingi, ukiongozwa na mwami na kuunganishwa na lugha na utamaduni wa Kinyarwanda. Ilitawaliwa na Ujerumani (takriban 1897) na, baada ya Vita vya Kwanza vya Dunia, kusimamiwa na Ubelgiji, ulioimarisha vitambulisho vya kikabila vilivyogawanya Wahutu, Watutsi na Watwa. Rwanda ilipata uhuru 1 Julai 1962. Kati ya 7 Aprili na katikati ya Julai 1994, Mauaji ya Halaiki dhidi ya Watutsi yaliua angalau watu 800,000 (makadirio mengine ni juu zaidi); yaliisha Rwandan Patriotic Front ilipochukua udhibiti, 4 Julai Kigali."),
   (["Every year Rwanda commemorates the genocide from 7 April (Kwibuka) with a mourning week and a 100-day remembrance period.", "Since 1994 Rwanda has focused on unity and reconciliation, using community 'Gacaca' courts (2002–2012) to try most genocide cases, and has rebuilt its economy and institutions.", "Rwanda is known as 'the land of a thousand hills' (Igihugu cy'imisozi igihumbi); Kigali is the capital; official languages include Kinyarwanda, English, French and Kiswahili.", "This is a short overview; for details, see the Kigali Genocide Memorial, the Commission for the Fight against Genocide (CNLG) and published historical research."],
    ["Chaque année le Rwanda commémore le génocide à partir du 7 avril (Kwibuka), avec une semaine de deuil et 100 jours de souvenir.", "Depuis 1994 le Rwanda met l'accent sur l'unité et la réconciliation, avec les tribunaux communautaires « Gacaca » (2002–2012) pour juger la plupart des cas, et a reconstruit son économie et ses institutions.", "Le Rwanda est « le pays des mille collines » ; Kigali est la capitale ; les langues officielles incluent le kinyarwanda, l'anglais, le français et le kiswahili.", "Ceci est un bref aperçu ; pour plus de détails, voir le Mémorial du génocide de Kigali, la CNLG et les recherches historiques publiées."],
    ["Buri mwaka u Rwanda rwibuka jenoside guhera ku wa 7 Mata (Kwibuka), hari icyumweru cy'icyunamo n'iminsi 100 yo kwibuka.", "Kuva mu 1994 u Rwanda rwibanze ku bumwe n'ubwiyunge, hakoreshejwe inkiko Gacaca (2002–2012) zakiriye ibyinshi mu manza, kandi rwongeye kubaka ubukungu n'inzego.", "U Rwanda ruzwi nk'«Igihugu cy'imisozi igihumbi»; Kigali ni umurwa mukuru; indimi zemewe zirimo Ikinyarwanda, Icyongereza, Igifaransa n'Igiswahili.", "Ni incamake; ku makuru arambuye reba Kigali Genocide Memorial, CNLG n'ubushakashatsi bwanditse ku mateka."],
    ["Kila mwaka Rwanda huadhimisha mauaji ya halaiki kuanzia 7 Aprili (Kwibuka), kukiwa na wiki ya maombolezo na siku 100 za kumbukumbu.", "Tangu 1994 Rwanda imejikita kwenye umoja na maridhiano, ikitumia mahakama za jamii 'Gacaca' (2002–2012) kusikiliza kesi nyingi, na kujenga upya uchumi na taasisi.", "Rwanda inajulikana kama 'nchi ya vilima elfu'; Kigali ni mji mkuu; lugha rasmi ni pamoja na Kinyarwanda, Kiingereza, Kifaransa na Kiswahili.", "Hii ni muhtasari; kwa maelezo zaidi tazama Kigali Genocide Memorial, CNLG na tafiti za kihistoria zilizochapishwa."])),

_e("digital_revolution", ["industrial_revolution", "cold_war", "what_is_ai"],
   ("What was the Digital Revolution and how did the internet begin?", "Qu'était la révolution numérique et comment Internet est-il né ?", "Digital Revolution yari iki kandi murandasi yatangiye ite?", "Mapinduzi ya Kidijitali yalikuwa nini na intaneti ilianzaje?"),
   ("digital revolution|history of the internet|who invented the internet|history of computers|world wide web|tim berners-lee|arpanet|first computer|information age|history of the smartphone",
    "revolution numerique|histoire d'internet|qui a invente internet|histoire des ordinateurs|world wide web|tim berners-lee|arpanet|premier ordinateur|ere de l'information|histoire du smartphone",
    "digital revolution|amateka ya murandasi|nde wahimbye murandasi|amateka ya mudasobwa|world wide web|tim berners-lee|arpanet|mudasobwa ya mbere|igihe cy'amakuru|amateka ya telefoni zigezweho",
    "mapinduzi ya kidijitali|historia ya intaneti|nani alivumbua intaneti|historia ya kompyuta|world wide web|tim berners-lee|arpanet|kompyuta ya kwanza|enzi ya habari|historia ya simu janja"),
   ("The Digital Revolution is the shift from mechanical and analogue technology to digital electronics and information, beginning in the mid-20th century. The transistor (1947) made small, cheap computers possible. The internet grew from ARPANET (1969), and Tim Berners-Lee invented the World Wide Web in 1989–91 at CERN, making the internet easy to use for everyone.",
    "La révolution numérique est le passage de la technologie mécanique et analogique à l'électronique et à l'information numériques, à partir du milieu du XXe siècle. Le transistor (1947) a rendu possibles des ordinateurs petits et peu chers. Internet est né d'ARPANET (1969), et Tim Berners-Lee a inventé le World Wide Web en 1989–91 au CERN, rendant Internet facile d'accès pour tous.",
    "Digital Revolution ni impinduka kuva ku ikoranabuhanga ry'imashini na analogue ujya kuri electronics na amakuru ya digitale, zatangiye hagati mu kinyejana cya 20. Transistor (1947) yatumye mudasobwa nto kandi zihendutse zishoboka. Murandasi yavuye muri ARPANET (1969), maze Tim Berners-Lee ahimba World Wide Web mu 1989–91 muri CERN, bituma murandasi yoroha ku bantu bose.",
    "Mapinduzi ya Kidijitali ni mabadiliko kutoka teknolojia ya mitambo na analogi kwenda elektroniki na taarifa za kidijitali, yaliyoanza katikati ya karne ya 20. Transistor (1947) ilifanya kompyuta ndogo na za bei nafuu ziwezekane. Intaneti ilikua kutoka ARPANET (1969), na Tim Berners-Lee alivumbua World Wide Web 1989–91 CERN, akiifanya intaneti iwe rahisi kwa kila mtu."),
   (["1940s: first electronic computers (ENIAC, 1945); 1947: transistor; 1958: integrated circuit.", "1971: microprocessor; 1970s–80s: personal computers (Apple II 1977, IBM PC 1981).", "1983: the internet adopts TCP/IP; 1991: the first website goes public; 1998: Google is founded.", "2007: iPhone popularised smartphones; today mobile internet, cloud computing and AI are reshaping work, trade and daily life."],
    ["Années 1940 : premiers ordinateurs électroniques (ENIAC, 1945) ; 1947 : transistor ; 1958 : circuit intégré.", "1971 : microprocesseur ; années 1970–80 : ordinateurs personnels (Apple II 1977, IBM PC 1981).", "1983 : Internet adopte TCP/IP ; 1991 : premier site web public ; 1998 : création de Google.", "2007 : l'iPhone popularise les smartphones ; aujourd'hui Internet mobile, cloud et IA transforment le travail, le commerce et la vie quotidienne."],
    ["Imyaka ya 1940: mudasobwa za mbere za electronic (ENIAC, 1945); 1947: transistor; 1958: integrated circuit.", "1971: microprocessor; 1970–80: mudasobwa bwite (Apple II 1977, IBM PC 1981).", "1983: murandasi yemeje TCP/IP; 1991: urubuga rwa mbere rutangazwa; 1998: Google ishingwa.", "2007: iPhone yamamaje smartphones; uyu munsi murandasi igendanwa, cloud na AI bihindura akazi, ubucuruzi n'imibereho."],
    ["Miaka ya 1940: kompyuta za kwanza za kielektroniki (ENIAC, 1945); 1947: transistor; 1958: saketi jumuishi.", "1971: microprocessor; miaka ya 1970–80: kompyuta binafsi (Apple II 1977, IBM PC 1981).", "1983: intaneti inapitisha TCP/IP; 1991: tovuti ya kwanza ya umma; 1998: Google inaanzishwa.", "2007: iPhone iliwezesha simu janja kuenea; leo intaneti ya simu, wingu na AI vinabadilisha kazi, biashara na maisha ya kila siku."])),
]
